  "Id": 174,
  "Title": "AKU-IED, Pakistan Graduates Awarded USAID Teacher Education Scholarships",
  "NewsSubTitle": null,
  "NewsSummary": "AKU-IED, P graduates to study in the USA.",
  "GlobalNews": false,
  "AlternateNewsTitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSubtitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSummary": null,
  "NewsContent": "<div class=\"ExternalClass4F9185AFAB394B72A22BFEFCEF7EFE96\"><div>The Office of the Provost is pleased to announce that four AKU-IED, Pakistan graduates have been awarded USAID scholarships to study in the USA.&#160;</div><div><br></div><div>Provost Greg Moran congratulated the faculty and staff of IED, Pakistan and wished the four graduates the greatest success in their studies, saying, &quot;This is another chapter in the amazing story of AKU and the difference it continues to make.&quot;</div><div><br></div><div>The graduates are&#58;</div><div><br></div><div>Mr. Syed Dhani Bux Shah Jillani, from Sukker, IED, P Class of 2008, selected for specialisation in Research and Assessment</div><div><br></div><div>Mr. Javed Iqbal, from Gilgit-Baltistan, IED, P Class of 2009, chosen for specialisation in Teacher Education</div><div><br></div><div>Mr. Shahid Hussain, from Quetta, Balochistan, IED, P Class of 2011, selected for specialisation in Curriculum Studies</div><div><br></div><div>Mr. Sher Ahmed, from Quetta, Balochistan, IED, P Class of 2014, selected for specialisation in Education &amp; Human Development, Educational Leadership and Administration</div></div>",
